# P18-V01 `EscapeNoneAscii` writer feature continuation

Timestamp: 2026-10-16 22:36 UTC
Plan: `plan/2026/09/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate.md` (unchanged)
Branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`
Starting revision: `ec43583d`
Implementation commit: `2dcbb98e`

## Changes

- Pinned Java oracle: RocketMQ client 5.5.1 at
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`; Fastjson2 2.0.63.
- Mapped `EscapeNoneAscii` for inherited body, route, and heartbeat serializer
  adapters. Source inspection of Fastjson2's UTF-8 writer and the invoked
  fixtures pin the current oracle runtime behavior: Latin-1 `é` remains raw,
  higher BMP characters are escaped with uppercase hex, and supplementary
  characters are emitted as UTF-16 surrogate escapes.
- Added invoked CheckClient and TopicRouteData Unicode cases, including
  newlines and escaped quotes; Rust checks both the shared route serializer and
  the special body serializer path.
- Updated the Phase 6 API/config crosswalk. Six of 48 writer features now have
  behavior mappings; 42 remain unmapped.

